{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#1516","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#1516","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#1516\",\"parent_revision\":\"ec0a185c86f32f2ace07142eef8d9f61246eade3e845cfe25d4894feb7a2a66a\",\"root_revision\":\"ec0a185c86f32f2ace07142eef8d9f61246eade3e845cfe25d4894feb7a2a66a\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: \\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: open\\nadded: \\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nThree independent cycle detection implementations exist: DependencyGraph.has_cycles() in dependencies.py (three-colour DFS, canonical), _has_cycles() in github_task.py (recursive DFS), and _has_cycle() in memory.py (iterative DFS). The new backends cannot use DependencyGraph.has_cycles() directly because it operates on Task Pydantic models, not TaskData TypedDicts. A shared adapter function _has_cycles_from_task_data(tasks: list[TaskData]) would eliminate two duplicate implementations.\\n\\n## Fact-Check\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n[VERIFIED] Three independent cycle detection implementations exist.\\n\\n- `dependencies.py:94-103` \u2014 `DependencyGraph.has_cycles()` delegates to `get_cycles()` which uses recursive three-colour DFS with cycle path reconstruction. Operates on `list[Task]` (Pydantic models).\\n- `github_task.py:184-201` \u2014 `_has_cycles(tasks: list[TaskData])` \u2014 recursive DFS, three-colour, no cycle path recovery. Operates on `list[TaskData]` (TypedDict).\\n- `memory.py:129-173` \u2014 `_has_cycle(tasks: list[TaskData])` \u2014 iterative DFS (stack-based), three-colour. Operates on `list[TaskData]` (TypedDict).\\n\\n[VERIFIED] The type mismatch is real: `DependencyGraph.__init__` takes `list[Task]` (line 48, `dependencies.py`). Neither backend can pass `list[TaskData]` to it without conversion.\\n\\n[VERIFIED] The two backend implementations differ in approach (recursive vs iterative) and in capability (no cycle path reconstruction vs canonical `get_cycles()` path). Both correctly detect cycles.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Issue Classification\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nType: refactor\\n\\nRoot cause: `DependencyGraph` was built for the Pydantic model layer (`Task`) before the TypedDict-based backend layer (`TaskData`) existed. No adapter between the two type layers was created when `github_task.py` and `memory.py` were added, so each backend wrote its own cycle check.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Files\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/core/dependencies.py:40-149` \u2014 canonical `DependencyGraph` (Pydantic model layer); `has_cycles()` at line 94\\n- `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/core/backends/github_task.py:184-201` \u2014 duplicate `_has_cycles()` to remove\\n- `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/core/backends/memory.py:129-173` \u2014 duplicate `_has_cycle()` to remove; called at line 568\\n</div>\\n\\n## Impact\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- Any bug or semantic change in cycle detection must be applied to three places.\\n- `_has_cycles` in `github_task.py` (recursive, no stack depth guard) is susceptible to `RecursionError` on large plans; `_has_cycle` in `memory.py` (iterative) is not. This silent divergence will produce different behaviour for deeply nested plans.\\n- The canonical `get_cycles()` which returns cycle paths is unavailable to both backends \u2014 callers that want cycle details (not just a boolean) must also duplicate the logic.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Dependencies\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nThis issue and #1517 share work: `get_plan_status` in both backends calls the cycle detection function directly. Resolving #1516 first (or in the same PR) is a prerequisite for cleanly resolving #1517 \u2014 `get_plan_status` aggregation should call the new shared helper, not the removed private functions.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] A module-level function `_has_cycles_from_task_data(tasks: list[TaskData]) -> bool` exists in a shared location (e.g. `sam_schema/core/backends/_shared.py` or inline in `dependencies.py`) with full TypedDict-typed signature \u2014 no `cast()` over TypedDict, no `object` or `Any`.\\n- [ ] `github_task._has_cycles` is removed and all call sites use the shared function.\\n- [ ] `memory._has_cycle` is removed and all call sites use the shared function.\\n- [ ] The shared function is iterative (matches memory.py's approach) to avoid `RecursionError` on large task graphs.\\n- [ ] Existing tests for cycle detection in both backends continue to pass.\\n- [ ] `uv run prek run --files <changed files>` exits 0.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Effort\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nEstimate: S\\nReasoning: Two functions to delete, one to create, two call sites to update. No schema changes, no API surface changes. Iterative DFS implementation already exists in `memory.py` \u2014 can be extracted with minor adaptation.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **maintainer of the codebase**, I want to **cycle detection implemented independently in github_task.py and memory.py \u2014 dependencies.py has canonical version** so that **the code is cleaner and more maintainable**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Simplify review of P912 \u2014 .tmp/scratch/reports/simplify-quality-P912.md\\n- **Priority**: P2\\n- **Added**: 2026-04-05\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n\\n---\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"0e93b132bace66c0f803c8e7ce6fd2bd832c9a847da4f75970fb07e9175392b6\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABSdr-Tw\"}"}